course: dictionary
lesson: 8505
title: Names and special words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are names, and a name starts with a capital letter. «European eels swim thousands of kilometres to the Sargasso Sea to lay eggs.» Here the Sargasso Sea is a place, a part of the Atlantic Ocean.
explain: The same word can also name a plant. Sargasso can mean a brown seaweed that floats in large mats. To know which meaning an author wants, read the words around it. Swim, lay eggs and sea tell you the word is a place.
explain: Ask yourself: is this a thing, a place or a name? A good check is to swap in another place name, such as the Pacific Ocean. If the sentence still makes sense, the word is a place.
fact: The Sargasso Sea is a part of the North Atlantic Ocean.
fact: The Sargasso Sea has no coast around it, so no land touches its edges.
fact: Sargasso, or sargassum, is a brown seaweed that floats in large mats.
fact: Baby turtles shelter in the floating seaweed.
fact: Eels from Europe and North America swim to the Sargasso Sea to lay eggs.
exercise: «European eels swim thousands of kilometres to the Sargasso Sea to lay eggs.» Is the Sargasso Sea a place or a seaweed? | A ship that sails the ocean | A seaweed that floats in mats | *A place, a sea in the Atlantic | A kind of eel
exercise: In «European eels swim thousands of kilometres to the Sargasso Sea to lay eggs», what do the eels do there? | *Lay eggs | Build a castle | Catch fish for dinner | Sleep on the beach
exercise: Which word in this sentence is a name with a capital letter? «European eels swim thousands of kilometres to the Sargasso Sea.» | *Sargasso | swim | kilometres | eels
test: Which of these is the name of a place? | sargassum | *the Sargasso Sea | seaweed | mats
test: «The babies drift back on ocean currents.» What does this tell you about the babies? | They stay in the Sargasso Sea for ever | *They are carried back by the moving water | They fly back to Europe | They walk back over land
exam: Which is true of the Sargasso Sea? | *It has no coast around it | It is a river in Africa | It is a beach in the Caribbean | It is a kind of eel
